  "answer_core": "Run a pre-buy test this week with the three interested customers: give them a named price and ask for a three-month prepay commitment. Set a written pass/fail bar upfront—e.g., at least two of three commit—and bound the decision window to 14 days. During that window, check competitive dynamics and the migration cost away from your current product; if the new workflow faces a saturated market or the migration is prohibitively expensive, treat that as a separate stop condition regardless of the test result.\n\nHave the hard conversations immediately because they unlock your ability to decide. Tell your CS employee now that you are exploring a pivot, that the current role would likely end if you switch products, and that you have a severance plan ready. Tell your former co-founder the plan as a courtesy—she is passive with 15%—but do not treat the conversation as a request for permission.\n\nIf the test passes and the competitive/migration check clears, pivot: use the prepay cash to fund a transition plan for your 22 current customers (freeze features, set a sunset date, or offer a migration path). If the test fails or the check reveals prohibitive risk, do not pivot; keep the current product alive and use the remaining runway to find another path.",
